  message: "Done in PR #2394. The fixture writes a second layout (one class per file, R, D, B, Child, S each in a file of its own, made visible the way each language does it) for all 17 languages, with the same callers, the four arms (the decoy's FILE order is the arm) and a second table MATRIX_SPLIT in test_call_resolution_matrix.py. Also added, as the item asked: three same-named candidates (THIRD: 19 cells move, all to unresolved or no_edge), and, from step 1, the same-variable callers. Beyond the item: a qualified-call column and the resolved_by mark behind every cell (MARKS, MARKS_SPLIT). RESULT: 14 of 17 languages answer the same in both layouts; csharp, groovy and objc do not (every same_file bind is unresolved across files). Guess cells: 28 in the one-file table, 12 in the split table, all 12 in the import and qual columns. Measured twice, identical; identical with file enumeration forced ascending and descending. NOT DONE: 12 of the 17 programs are not compiled (no toolchain on the machine): typescript, java, kotlin, scala, groovy, csharp, go, swift, objc, ruby, php, lua. Reproduce: python packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/_call_matrix_fixture.py"  # 1c38
